WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.021
villagers gathered around Gau.

2
00:00:15.461 --> 00:00:16.763
He groaned in pain.

3
00:00:17.944 --> 00:00:21.627
Suddenly some women appeared, howling and screaming.

4
00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:26.012
The villagers began to clap loudly and chant.

5
00:00:27.568 --> 00:00:31.791
A man wearing bracelets on his wrists and ankles jumped into the fire.

6
00:00:31.811 --> 00:00:34.652
"Wow!" said Vinnie.

7
00:00:35.993 --> 00:00:39.435
The man began dancing and jumped in and out of the fire.

8
00:00:40.776 --> 00:00:44.678
He waved his arms above his head and then moved over to Gau.

9
00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:48.661
The healer placed his hands on Gau's leg.

10
00:00:50.322 --> 00:00:53.824
The villagers clapped harder, and the women screamed louder.

11
00:00:55.304 --> 00:00:57.545
"Oh, Twi, I'm scared!"

12
00:00:58.246 --> 00:00:59.086
cried Mandy.

13
00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:03.269
"Shh, Mandy," whispered Twi.

14
00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:07.171
"Yeah, Mandy, cool it," said Vinnie.

15
00:01:08.752 --> 00:01:10.753
Soon, everything got quiet.

16
00:01:12.014 --> 00:01:14.916
Gau sat up, and Kashe walked over to him.

17
00:01:16.197 --> 00:01:18.198
The other villagers gathered around.

18
00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.640
An old man was sitting close by.

19
00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:26.871
He was holding a rock and dipping his fingers into some kind of paint.

20
00:01:28.252 --> 00:01:30.434
He started drawing something on the rock.

21
00:01:30.454 --> 00:01:32.876
"What's he doing?"

22
00:01:33.677 --> 00:01:34.818
Mandy asked Twi.

23
00:01:34.838 --> 00:01:39.942
"He is recording the healing on a rock," explained Twi.

24
00:01:39.962 --> 00:01:44.285
"His picture proves our healers have great power.

25
00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:48.989
We use these rocks to tell the story to our children."

26
00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:52.612
"Stories?" asked Vinnie.

27
00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:55.621
"Yes," said Twi.

28
00:01:56.802 --> 00:01:59.083
"Sometimes we have bigger stories to tell.

29
00:02:00.404 --> 00:02:02.084
So we put them on bigger rocks."

30
00:02:03.645 --> 00:02:05.606
"Come," Twi's mother called.

31
00:02:06.847 --> 00:02:08.828
"We have delicious mongongo!"

32
00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:11.189
Everyone cheered.

33
00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:15.712
Twi brought over two bowls for Vinnie and Mandy.

34
00:02:17.253 --> 00:02:18.293
Mandy took a sip.

35
00:02:19.954 --> 00:02:21.095
"It's wonderful!"

36
00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:24.401
she said.

37
00:02:25.902 --> 00:02:28.944
Kashe came over and sat beside Vinnie and Mandy.

38
00:02:30.245 --> 00:02:32.686
They all watched some boys playing a game.

39
00:02:34.147 --> 00:02:39.231
They were throwing long wooden sticks at a round target made out of woven grass.

40
00:02:39.251 --> 00:02:44.795
"The little ones are already practicing to be good hunters," said Kashe.

41
00:02:44.815 --> 00:02:48.358
"One day you'll be a fine hunter too, Vinnie."

42
00:02:48.378 --> 00:02:54.538
"Vinnie," said Mandy, "I think I know what the glowing thing is."

43
00:02:56.019 --> 00:02:56.659
"What is it?"

44
00:02:57.139 --> 00:02:57.760
asked Vinnie.

45
00:02:59.381 --> 00:03:01.402
He didn't want to take the photo out.

46
00:03:02.823 --> 00:03:04.404
All the villagers would see it.

47
00:03:04.424 --> 00:03:06.786
"It's a rock.

48
00:03:07.206 --> 00:03:12.090
I saw it when I was gathering mongongo nuts with Twi," Mandy said.

49
00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:16.773
"But you didn't return home," Vinnie pointed out.

50
00:03:18.294 --> 00:03:19.595
She thought for a moment.

51
00:03:19.615 --> 00:03:21.116
"I know.

52
00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:22.780
It's strange."

53
00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:28.682
"You should get some rest," said Kashe, turning to the children.

54
00:03:28.702 --> 00:03:31.263
"We are moving our village tomorrow."

55
00:03:32.923 --> 00:03:34.444
"Where?" asked Vinnie.

56
00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:40.866
"To a place with fresh water," Kashe answered, and went inside a hut.

57
00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:48.788
"Vinnie," Mandy whispered, "We can't go with them—we have to get home!"

58
00:03:50.468 --> 00:03:54.429
The children quietly left the village and went toward the cave.

59
00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:57.150
Nobody saw them leave.

60
00:03:58.530 --> 00:03:59.971
Vinnie took out the photo.

61
00:04:00.451 --> 00:04:01.571
It was glowing blue.

62
00:04:01.591 --> 00:04:05.192
"We're close," said Mandy.

63
00:04:06.532 --> 00:04:10.113
They walked over to the painted rock just inside the cave.

64
00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:12.094
"This is it!"

65
00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:13.254
she said.

66
00:04:14.595 --> 00:04:16.735
She could see animals and dancing men.

67
00:04:18.096 --> 00:04:19.436
Vinnie looked at the photo.

68
00:04:20.664 --> 00:04:23.585
"But why weren't you sent home when you were here with Twi?"

69
00:04:23.605 --> 00:04:28.047
"I don't Mandy began.

70
00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:34.230
"Wait—maybe because we always have to go photo traveling together!"

71
00:04:34.991 --> 00:04:35.631
she cried.

72
00:04:36.811 --> 00:04:38.472
The photo was glowing red.

73
00:04:38.492 --> 00:04:41.254
"That's it!"

74
00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:42.554
shouted Vinnie.

75
00:04:43.935 --> 00:04:46.156
The children fell down the dark tunnel.
